reagent-name-bz = BZ
reagent-desc-bz = A potent hallucinogen that also puts Slimes to sleep.

reagent-name-healium = Healium
reagent-desc-healium = A powerful sedative with regenerative properties.

reagent-name-nitrium = Nitrium
reagent-desc-nitrium = A powerful stimulant; when inhaled, it boosts speed and stamina.

reagent-name-pluoxium = Pluoxium
reagent-desc-pluoxium = A gas that saturates the blood with large amounts of oxygen without acting as an oxidizer.

reagent-name-hyper-nob = Hyper-Noblium
reagent-desc-hyper-nob = The noblest of all gases. Large quantities of Hyper-Noblium actively prevent chemical reactions from occurring.

reagent-name-proto-nitrate = Proto-Nitrate
reagent-desc-proto-nitrate = An unstable gas that reacts differently depending on the specific gases it encounters.

reagent-name-zauker = Zauker
reagent-desc-zauker = An extremely toxic gas; its production is strictly regulated—a measure taken in addition to the inherent difficulty of manufacturing it. It decomposes rapidly upon contact with nitrogen.

reagent-name-halon = Halon
reagent-desc-halon = A powerful fire suppressant. At high temperatures, it absorbs oxygen and cools the surrounding area.

reagent-name-helium = Helium
reagent-desc-helium = An inert gas produced through the synthesis of hydrogen and its derivatives.

reagent-name-anti-nob = Anti-Noblium
reagent-desc-anti-nob = We still don't know what it does, but it's expensive.

reagent-name-electrovae = Electrovae
reagent-desc-electrovae = An ominously humming gas.

reagent-name-charged-electrovae = Charged Electrovae
reagent-desc-charged-electrovae = An electrically charged gas. It causes a tingling sensation on the skin.

